# apps/claude-remotion — API keys
#
# Copy to .env in this directory and fill in what you need:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. .env.example is not — never put a real key in this file.
#
# YOU DO NOT NEED ANY KEY TO START. These all run with nothing set:
#     npm run hello    render the zero-key hello-world (proves your install works)
#     npm run dev      open Remotion Studio and preview compositions
#     npm run lint     type-check
# Keys are needed only when a step generates voice, music, images or a script —
# that is, when it calls a paid service.


# --- Text-to-speech and script generation -------------------------------------------------
# Required for the daily AI Top 5 edition (make-ai-top5.mjs --with-audio) and for the
# how-it-works voiceover. Roughly $0.02-0.03 of TTS per video at ~$15 per 1M characters.
OPENAI_API_KEY=


# --- ElevenLabs voice (optional) ----------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. If this is set it takes precedence over OpenAI for TTS, unless you override with
# TTS_PROVIDER=openai. Billed in credits at roughly 1 credit per character, so a video is
# ~1,700 credits on eleven_multilingual_v2 — materially more expensive than OpenAI TTS.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=


# --- ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: not needed --------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately not listed as a variable above: nothing in this app reads it as a key, so
# setting it has no effect. It is mentioned only because it used to be actively rejected by
# the container render worker, which has since been removed.


# --- Spend guard (optional) ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Ceiling for the voiceover step, checked before each paid call rather than after it.
# Defaults to 3000 credits if unset; the worst real session measured here was ~1,582, so the
# default is a runaway guard and not a budget. The refusal message names these overrides.
# PB_BUDGET_CREDITS=3000
# PB_BUDGET_USD=
